# The Content-Security-Policy is not here: it is written into the built page
# by vite.config.js, which knows the Supabase address the build talks to.
#
# Cloudflare Pages reads this at deploy time. It mirrors the headers block in
# vercel.json, so the site is equally locked down on either host.
#
# RankUp lives at rankup.<your domain>, beside MTRX Horizyn's other sites on
# the same parent domain. It shares nothing with them: no cookie (RankUp sets
# none), no CORS header (none here, none from /api), no Service-Worker-Allowed
# (the worker's scope is this site), and Origin-Agent-Cluster keeps the page
# in an agent cluster of its own, so document.domain cannot be used to reach
# into it from a sibling. tests/isolation.mjs checks all of it.
#
# "! Access-Control-Allow-Origin" takes away the "*" Cloudflare Pages puts on
# every static file by default. Those files hold nothing private (anyone can
# download them, and "*" never covers a request with credentials), but RankUp
# has no reason to let another site's page read them, a sibling's included.
# Vercel adds the same "*" to static files and has no way to take it away;
# the same reasoning makes that harmless, and /api sends no CORS header there
# either.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Origin-Agent-Cluster: ?1
  ! Access-Control-Allow-Origin

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
